%% MUPP-043 Secret Santa: anonymous chat
%% How a giver and their receiver talk without the receiver learning who the giver is, and how a message reaches the other side by mail.
flowchart TD
    S[Group started, draw in ss_draw] --> B[Unread: a small icon with a dot on the card, R5. The chat bubble is inside the opened lists, R1 R2]
    B -->|side: giver or receiver, never an id| O[Open: the pair is read from the draw with the member from the cookie, R4]
    O --> L[Answer is only mine + text per message, R3]
    O --> U[The other side's messages are marked read, R5]
    L --> W[Write 1 to 500 characters, either side first, several in a row, R1 R2]
    W --> I[Saved with from_giver and no time shown]
    I --> J[Job every 10 minutes: POST /api/santa-mails]
    J --> C{oldest unmailed message waited 10 minutes?}
    C -->|no| Z[Collected, nothing sent]
    C -->|yes, and something is still unread| M[Take the mark, send mail 6 or 7 to the other side: names the group, nobody, no text, R6]
    C -->|all already read| N[Marked mailed, nothing sent]
    M -->|mail fails| R[Mark put back, tried again next run]
    X[Draw stopped or started again, group deleted, yearly cleanup] --> G[Conversations deleted, R7]
